		{
			"id": "memo_group",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Memos** (7) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[S6M1]] — multi-notation RE breaks at translation gaps\n- [[L1M4]] — switching notation family shifts the modelling frame\n- [[L3M7]] — different families need different tool affordances\n- [[S5M2]] — examples and public feedback calibrate detail\n- [[S7M5]] — new syntax at the switch; a real reader later\n- [[S8M3]] — similar families confuse; paid work drains care\n- [[S10M1]] — BPMN-to-UML breaks when treated as the same model",
			"x": -440,
			"y": 206,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 276,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "code_group",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "**Codes** (23) — Ctrl+hover a link to preview\n\n- [[L1-C01]] — course covers BPMN SysML and feature models\n- [[L1-C12]] — BPMN expressive detail makes learning harder\n- [[L1-C13]] — shift to feature models changes modelling mindset\n- [[L3-C24]] — BPMN teaching relies on collaborative traceable tools\n- [[L3-C25]] — BPMN richer than activity-diagram analogy suggests\n- [[S5-C01]] — sequence diagram notation and granularity get messy\n- [[S5-C04]] — drafts version one without waiting for demo\n- [[S5-C05]] — teacher examples calibrate acceptable detail level\n- [[S5-C08]] — comfortable sharing work-in-progress publicly\n- [[S6-C01]] — UML class diagram lost trace from goals\n- [[S6-C02]] — nobody explained how much iStar survives in UML\n- [[S6-C08]] — mindset resets moving between notation families\n- [[S6-C14]] — wants explicit continuous translation example\n- [[S7-C01]] — same idea taught with different course notations\n- [[S7-C14]] — switching notations confuses syntax not starting\n- [[S7-C15]] — thesis reader made modelling a priority\n- [[S8-C08]] — similar notations confuse until an example sits beside\n- [[S8-C09]] — paid tutoring lowered interest more than other courses\n- [[S10-C02]] — too-direct BPMN-to-UML translation of an external party\n- [[S10-C03]] — models answer different questions\n- [[S10-C04]] — knows the meaning not how to say it in this language\n- [[S10-C05]] — names carry over process structure does not\n- [[S10-C06]] — traceability taught but not done rigorously",
			"x": 600,
			"y": 206,
			"width": 520,
			"height": 724,
			"color": "5"
		},
		{
			"id": "explainer",
			"type": "text",
			"text": "What this means\n\nSwitching from one notation family to another is hard. What you knew in the first notation does not transfer cleanly: names may carry while structure does not, lookalike diagrams confuse, or syntax is new even when starting is not. Models answer different questions. S9 is not used here.",
			"x": 80,
